ating world in which he lived. James numbered among his correspondents the writers William Dean Howells, Henry Adams, Robert Louis Stevenson, H. G.\n\nWells and Edith Wharton, as well as presidents and prime ministers, painters and great ladies, actresses and bishops. These letters provide a rich and fascinating source for James's views on his own works, on the literary craft, on sex, politics and friendship, and collectively constitute, in Philip Horne's own words, James's 'real and best biography'.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":14,"revision":14,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-09-19T03:44:23.692443"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-07T09:50:05.962935"}},{"publishers":["Folcroft Library Editions"],"physical_format":"Unknown Binding","subtitle":"Letters to A.C. Benson and Auguste Monod","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-04-30T11:32:04.683988"},"source_records":["amazon:0841417695"],"title":"Henry James","created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T20:50:18.033121"},"isbn_13":["9780841417694"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0841417695"],"publish_date":"1976","key":"/books/OL11527835M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL21001A"}],"latest_revision":5,"oclc_numbers":["2542357"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL276471W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["19th century","Authors, American","Authors, English","Benson, Arthur Christopher","Correspondence","James, Henry","Monod, Auguste"],"revision":5},{"publishers":["Dutton"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["2968410"],"librarything":["733753"]},"subtitle":"Selected Fiction","weight":"8 ounces","physical_format":"Paperback","key":"/books/OL7770273M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL21001A"}],"contributions":["Leon Edel (Editor)"],"subjects":["Fiction / General"],"source_records":["amazon:0525471405:bv:1856238686:140851","ia:selectedfiction0000jame_k2f7","bwb:9780525471400","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.00.20150123.full.mrc